WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.150
(groaning)
(soft dramatic music)

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.140
- Just when we thought
Spider-Man was going

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.810
to be the new face of the
Marvel Cinematic Universe

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:12.160
for years to come a stand
off between Disney and Sony

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.720
could put a stop to it.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.190
So what does this mean for the future

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:17.200
of the MCU and Spider-Man?

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.390
Let's discuss right now on The Ketchup.

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:20.900
I can't believe I'm saying this

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.680
but after failed negotiations

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.960
Marvel Studios President, Kevin
Feige, will not be involved

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.250
in the next two planned Spider-Man movies.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.180
And the character,

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.500
whose film rights are
held by Sony Pictures,

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.140
will no longer be available
to Marvel Studios.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:35.650
This isn't the Daily Bugle guys!

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:37.420
This is happening and it's wild.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:38.280
- [Peter] I don't understand.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.390
- As far as what this means for the MCU,

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:42.120
well all that talk about Spider-Man

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.570
being the next Iron
Man in "Far From Home,"

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:46.990
plus Nick Fury wanting him
to help out up in space

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:48.980
means he was going to be a major player

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.460
in phase five or six.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.470
So this is gonna be a tough
web for them to untangle.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:54.530
And this whole time I thought

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.580
Spider-Man ghosting Nick Fury was a joke!

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.230
- You do not ghost Nick Fury!

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:00.160
- Let's talk about the
future of Spider-Man.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.050
Since having your own cinematic universe

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:03.340
is totally a thing now

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:06.130
Sony's planning to expand
upon the Spider-Verse,

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:08.890
which has about 900
characters to choose from.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:10.260
That's a lot of characters!

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.160
And coming off of the heels

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.267
of 2018's certified fresh,
Oscar winning animated movie

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:16.170
"Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse,"

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:17.880
Sony also has a sequel to "Venom,"

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.110
starring Tom Hardy, coming next year.

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:22.810
And projects for characters
like Kraven the Hunter,

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.910
Silver Sable and Black Cat
are also in development.

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:28.290
Plus a movie with Morbius
the Living Vampire

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:31.077
played by Jared Leto
is also coming in 2021.

00:01:31.077 --> 00:01:33.300
- Blah, blah, blah.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.610
- As for the upcoming Spider-Man movies

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:38.690
even with Tom Holland and
director Jon Watts returning

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:40.290
it might get kinda weird

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:41.760
not being able to reference things

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.650
like Peter's journey with the MCU,

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.600
his connections to Stark Industries,

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:46.860
not to mention the motivation

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.860
behind Jake Gyllenhaal's Mysterio,

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:51.140
and on top of all of that,
there's poor Tom Holland

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:52.730
stuck in the middle of all of this.

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:54.260
And I think we all know how he feels

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:57.050
about playing Spider-Man
because, well, he told me.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.460
- I honestly would play Spider-Man

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:00.110
until like I can't walk anymore.

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:02.540
- Basically this all comes down to money!

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:05.180
Disney, who owns Marvel,
wants to do an even split

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:06.760
of all future Spider-Man films.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.860
But Sony said no and wants to keep

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:10.073
the current deal where it stands

00:02:10.073 --> 00:02:13.290
which means Marvel gets a
small percentage of the gross.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:14.710
In other words, they just don't want

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:16.450
to share their biggest franchise.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:17.820
And this is despite the fact

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.160
that the Fiege produced
"Spider-Man Far From Home" film

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.000
recently became Sony's
highest grossing movie ever!

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.400
And maybe that's just it.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.890
Looking to the near future,

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:29.500
Marvel's phase four films
slated for the next couple years

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.690
actually don't have
much to do with Spidey.

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:32.547
The upcoming sequel,

00:02:32.547 --> 00:02:34.530
"Doctor Strange in the
Multiverse of Madness,"

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.870
will most likely take
place far from Manhattan

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.430
where Peter was just revealed
and blamed for everything.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:40.960
So, I guess he'll just be in hiding

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.200
till he can clear his name?

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.460
I mean, literally!

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:44.880
And that could mean Shang-Chi,

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.450
with the movie coming in 2021,

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:49.080
will take a more central role in the MCU.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.400
And Sony is definitely feeling the heat

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.790
and shouldering most of
the blame on social media.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:56.417
So they put out a series
of tweets saying, quote,

00:02:56.417 --> 00:02:58.047
"Much of today's news about Spider-Man

00:02:58.047 --> 00:03:00.137
"has mischaracterized recent discussions

00:03:00.137 --> 00:03:02.917
"about Kevin Feige's
involvement in the franchise.

00:03:02.917 --> 00:03:05.527
"We are disappointed but
respect Disney's decision

00:03:05.527 --> 00:03:07.562
"not to have him continue
as a lead producer

00:03:07.562 --> 00:03:10.217
"of our next live action Spider-Man film.

00:03:10.217 --> 00:03:11.907
"Kevin is terrific and we are grateful

00:03:11.907 --> 00:03:13.727
"for his help and guidance and appreciate

00:03:13.727 --> 00:03:16.930
"the path he has helped put us
on, which we will continue."

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.130
But whether it's Disney
or Sony that's to blame,

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.400
it doesn't really matter,

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.760
because it's the fan's
who are losing, right?

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.770
I mean even Hawkeye
himself, Jeremy Renner,

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.987
is hoping this gets resolved,
by saying on Instagram,

00:03:26.987 --> 00:03:28.977
"Hey Sony Pictures, we want Spider-Man

00:03:28.977 --> 00:03:31.700
"back to Stan Lee and
Marvel please, thank you".

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:33.970
Who knows guys, maybe
we'll get some answers soon

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:36.700
seeing as Disney's D23
Expo is this weekend?

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.060
- [Peter] Come on man, please.

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:40.250
- But it is time for me
to kick it over to you now

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:42.420
because I have a lot of questions!

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:44.870
What do you think about
an MCU without Spider-Man?

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.180
Or Spider-Man without the MCU?

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:49.760
Are you #savespiderman or are you excited

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.120
to see what the Sony
Spider-Verse has to offer?

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.380
Or are you just waiting
for the next DC movie?

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.140
And did Iron Man die for nothing?

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.510
Let us know in the comment
section all your feelings!

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.160
And for all the latest MCU news

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:03.150
head on over to rottentomatoes.com.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.410
As always, thanks for
watching our show The Ketchup.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.420
I'm Naz Perez and I'm going to send

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:10.043
all my therapy bills
to Sony and Disney now.

00:04:10.043 --> 00:04:12.626
(upbeat music)

